{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/769134-deadliest-supernatural-warrior-the-setup","id":769134,"title":"Deadliest supernatural warrior: the setup","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-11-19T05:21:26-08:00","id":769134,"title":"Deadliest supernatural warrior: the setup","content":"<img src=\"https://dl.dropboxusercontent.com/u/23843264/Permanent/VWFGRougp400y.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> A long, long time ago, a contributor on this forum promised to upgrade his combat algorithm to allow many different types of strategies (including clinches) in a battle between werewolves and vampires.<br /> <br /> That contributor is me, and that promise is now coming to pass, after a long period lost failing to get neural nets to work.<br /> <br /> I'll be comparing the combat power of:<br /> <br /> Humans, Wraiths, Risen, Hunters, Demon, Mummies, Ghouls, Dhampirs, Kuei-Jin, Mage, Changelings, Vampires, Werewolves, some Fera, and... <b>one mystery guest</b>. It should be quite exciting ^_^<br /> <br /> And at the end of it, I'll reveal the <b>ultimate secret of combat victory</b> in the world of darkness... (which may be, or may not be, what you're expecting)<br /> <br /> <br /> The rest of this post is just explaining the rules and assumptions I'm using for this battle. If any of the rules seem unfair or objectionable, the time to object is now, because it takes several days (at least) to run each battle. Most of the rules are standard, others are ones I'd had to piece together, some are just there to make the decision tree tractable.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4851-cheesefondue","name":"Cheesefondue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"275"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-19T05:22:14-08:00","id":769136,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Basic rules:</span></span></span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\">*I'm using the vampire V20 rules for combat. Main reason: it's that or werewolf, and vampire doesn't have different difficulties for defending against different weapons.</span></span></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">*The exception is the bite rules, which are better in werewolf. Since werewolves can bite all the time, and vampires only when clinched, it seems more natural to stick with the werewolf rules.<br /> *Characters cannot split their main action into multiple attacks against the same target (what, the cheatin' caitiff with a dice pool of 16, you want to let her have 16 attacks?!?)</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">*Clinch is in. A character can choose to clinch another; if successful, they deal strength damage, and all other actions, from both characters, are cancelled for the turn. From that point onwards, there is no difference between the two characters in the clinch.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">*In clinch, characters can inflict strength damage, bite (if they have the required fangs), or try to break the clinch. Breaking the clinch cancels all other actions from both characters.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">*The vampire has the option of the Kiss if in a clinch. The rules state that vampires only have the ability to resist the Kiss by making a </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Self-Control/</span></span></span><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Instinct roll of difficulty 8. I've changed this to a permanent willpower roll of difficulty 8 (since every creature has willpower, and it's generally higher that self-control), doable by anyone.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">*The basic combat manoeuvres are punch/claw, bite, clinch, and armed attack. No other moves have been included.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">*The characters can spend willpower to get an automatic success on an attack or defence.</span></span></span><br /> *On a botch, the character damages themselves with their weapon.<br /> *It's hard to tell whether the various supernaturals that can heal, can do so in combat. My reading of it is that only shapeshifters and wraiths can heal themselves in combat.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">*All types can spend a willpower to ignore wound penalties for a turn.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">*Characters in frenzy avoid all wound penalties.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">*Characters in frenzy can spend a willpower to be able to make defensive actions that turn.<br /> *Initiative does not change in the course of combat. This means additional wound penalties incurred in combat will not affect initiative until the next turn.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">*This also means that adding extra celerity actions can't change initiative, even though it changes dexterity and hence initiative rating.. Therefore, as a compromise, celerity will be counted as half its value (rounded down) for initiative purposes.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">*A vampire with celerity must be able to spend the first blood point for extra actions within their generation limits; subsequent spending can go beyond the limit.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">*Humans (and any character unable to soak lethal damage) get dazed if they take more damage than their stamina. So do werewolves, as this is specifically listed in their rules. Otherwise, supernaturals get dazed if they get damaged by more than their stamina+2.</span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4851,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4851-cheesefondue","user":"Cheesefondue","date":". 12-02-2015, 09:26 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4851-cheesefondue","name":"Cheesefondue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"275"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-19T05:23:11-08:00","id":769139,"title":"","content":"<br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Character/situation rules:</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">*In each supernatural splat, there will be one basic non-combat character (generally 2/3/3 on physical stats, with 2 in brawl/melee/acrobatics) and one broken power-character.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">*Each character is a beginning character. The broken character has been given 7 extra freebie points from non-combat related flaws.<br /> *EDIT: Since some character types (Vampires, Changelings, Shapeshifters) benefit from backgrounds in single combat, while others do not, no-one gets free background points (but they can purchase it with freebies).</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">*Each character has the option of a strength+2 lethal short sword, which they will take unless they have better natural weapons. Strength+1 aggravated claws are considered better natural weapons than the short sword.</span></span></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">*How to deal with the weapon when in a clinch? The compromise solution is that characters can't use weapons when clinched, but pick them up again - or have then attacked to their hand on a strap - if ever the clinch is broken.<br /> *The combat takes place in a room, which the combatants cannot escape and where they can reach each other every turn.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">*Each character gets one turn to prepare. The preparation is done without knowing their opponent, so is always the same.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">*Anything attempted during the preparation is assumed to succeed (eg Visage of Fenris). When the number of successes is relevant (eg the Hunter's Foresee power), I assume they have the whole number number of successes closest to their average successes.<br /> *Normal humans, Hunters, and Mages cannot soak lethal damage. All other types can. Aggravated damage can only be soaked by shapeshifters and those with relevant abilities.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">*Each combat lasts up to 30 turns.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">*If the combat ends in a draw (30 turns without a winner or simultaneous kills), one winner is assigned randomly. Each combat is thus a win or a loss.</span></span><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4851,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4851-cheesefondue","user":"Cheesefondue","date":". 11-30-2015, 12:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4851-cheesefondue","name":"Cheesefondue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"275"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-19T05:24:04-08:00","id":769140,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">The algorithm:</span></span></span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">*The main problem here is exponential growth. Suppose each character faces five yes/no decisions each turn, in a combat that lasts 5 turns. Then there are 33,554,432 different strategies they can take. If the decision depend on things like the amount of damage they take, or the blood they have left, or what decisions the other character makes, the number of possibilities explodes. Worse than that, since the outcomes have some randomness in them, each strategy has to be run against each other one hundreds of times.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">*So the question was how to test the best strategies without testing them all. Methods of deep learning can be used here have a neural net learn the best strategy. But my neural net failed to stabilise.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">*So I decided to go for the second best approximation: each player would choose from a certain number of rigid strategies. Then I would compute the Nash equilibrium of these rigid strategies (roughly, which randomises mixes of rigid strategies would perform best), and use that to get the outcome.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">*Computing Nash equilibrium is normally difficult, but it's much easier if the game is zero sum, ie if each battle has a winner or a loser.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">The rigid strategies are as follows:</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">General facts:</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">*When they suffer from any wound penalty, characters capable of frenzy will frenzy (argument: this is the kind of situations where they might be required to pass a frenzy test, and anyone willing to fail a frenzy test will fail), and will thus avoid any further wound penalties. Recall that frenzied characters can spend willpower to attempt defensive actions.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">*If they suffer from any wound penalty and cannot frenzy, characters will spend willpower to ignore wound penalties.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">*When their opponent is dazed or stunned, they will attack with the maximal attacks they can.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">*Vampires and those able too boost stats with blood (or chi) follow the same rigid plan: if they can spend blood to boost (for instance, if they haven't spent it on celerity) they boost Dexterity to the maximum, then Strength to the maximum, then &quot;overboost&quot; Dexterity (Kuei-Jin, who cannot overboost, instead boost Stamina).</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">*The best attack and defence is chosen in each situation automatically.</span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">Unconditional strategy elements (number of options in brackets):</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">EDIT: since a preliminary analysis shows that all the best strategies involve spending willpower early, I've removed the option not to do so.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">(2) When not clinched, either best normal attack, or try to start a clinch.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">(2-3) When clinched, either try to break clinch, do best normal attack (strength damage or bite) or Kiss (vampires only).</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">(1-4) If character has the possibility of multiple attacks, add 0, 1, 50% of max number of attacks, or 100% of max number of attacks.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">(1-4) If character has the possibility of multiple defences, add 0, 1, 50% of max number of defences, or 100% of max number of defences.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">(1-6) Split main action between attack and defence. We don't need every option here: consider my broken Caitiff character, with a dice pool of 16 (!). It doesn't matter much whether they split it 9-7 or 8-8 between attack and defence. So there are a maximum of 7 different splits the character can try. Total defence is not possible here.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">Conditional strategy elements:</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">(2) If the opponent has chosen their actions that turn, and they have not included any defence, then either do the usual choices or go for all-out attack.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">(2) If the opponent has chosen multiple actions, or has yet to choose and has the possibility of multiple actions (due to unspent rage, blood+celerity, demon chi, etc...), or is a Hunter using all their conviction, then either do the usual or go for a total defence. This is the only way of getting total defence (one cannot win a battle purely with total defence).</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">*Each combination of rigid strategies is run a 100 times.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">*Therefore the most number of strategies available to a character is 2*3*4*4*6*2*2 = 2304. If two such characters fight each other, there will be 4608*4608=21,233,664 combinations, and hence </span></span>5,308,416<span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"> - over half a billion.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">*Typically, each fight between two specific characters takes a few days to run (though the two half billion battles will be much longer).</span></span><br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4851,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4851-cheesefondue","user":"Cheesefondue","date":". 11-30-2015, 12:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4851-cheesefondue","name":"Cheesefondue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"275"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-28T13:31:04-08:00","id":776176,"title":"","content":"My only concern so far is about only Wraiths and Shapeshifters healing in combat. On most supernaturals that can heal themselves, there are no reason whatsoever to think they can't heal in combat. Demons and Vampires I'm pretty sure that can heal in combat.<br /> <br /> Obviously, assuming you're talking about common powers, not special cases, like Disciplines or Lore. Those I would simply make into an action.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-28T21:40:36-08:00","id":776417,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/769134-deadliest-supernatural-warrior-the-setup?p=776176#post776176\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My only concern so far is about only Wraiths and Shapeshifters healing in combat. On most supernaturals that can heal themselves, there are no reason whatsoever to think they can't heal in combat. Demons and Vampires I'm pretty sure that can heal in combat.</div> </div> </div> </div>Reading the (newest) rules carefully, it seems only werewolves and wraiths can heal directly in combat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4851-cheesefondue","name":"Cheesefondue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"275"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-29T11:19:11-08:00","id":776688,"title":"","content":"Given that I don't have currently the newest rules with me, I won't argue that further, just remain skeptical.<br /> <br /> Could you reference the books, so I can look for them? I'm assuming V20 for Vampire, and I don't know yet of anything new for Demon.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-29T11:48:03-08:00","id":776704,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vampire the Masquerade 20th Anniversary</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">A vampire may spend one blood point to heal one normal (bashing or lethal) health level of damage. Characters must be resting and relatively inactive for this healing to take place, though this recovery is rapid: One blood point per turn may be spent to heal one health level, though vampires of lower Generations may heal as many health levels per turn as they can spend blood points.<br /> Note that blood expenditure is the only way that vampires can heal wounds. Just as their immortality prevents the Kindred from aging and dying naturally, so it also inhibits the recuperative processes natural to a living body.</div> </div> </div> </div>Vampires could potentially heal in combat, it would just be very risky.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-29T22:35:08-08:00","id":777007,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/769134-deadliest-supernatural-warrior-the-setup?p=776704#post776704\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Vampires could potentially heal in combat, it would just be very risky.</div> </div> </div> </div>You can't 'be resting' and also be 'in combat;' the two are mutually exclusive.<br /> <br /> Vamp healing seems worthless against Garou anyway, though. Agg damage op White Wolf pls nerf","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","name":"The Laughing Stranger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3695_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1010"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-30T00:14:55-08:00","id":777035,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Laughing Stranger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/769134-deadliest-supernatural-warrior-the-setup?p=777007#post777007\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You can't 'be resting' and also be 'in combat;' the two are mutually exclusive.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ghouls or other vampires occupy the opponents while you slink back and take a 'breather.' Maybe you're not in combat at that point, it doesn't matter. You're not attacking, no one's attacking you.<br /> <br /> It's not likely to work in one-on-one arena combat but is something you could potentially pull off in-game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-30T00:38:05-08:00","id":777040,"title":"","content":"Vampires can heal during combat (or other actions, as the book puts it), but they have to make a Stamina + Survival roll, difficulty 8. Page 258 of V20.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-30T05:21:41-08:00","id":777094,"title":"","content":"All in all.... I would say any Mage with Arete 6, avatar 4+ and a sphere at 5 has a very good chance to win any battle in his very first action, if he has some Arete to spare: Blast the enemy with a fitting spell!<br /> Turn time forward in &gt;&gt; mode, till he withers and dies/falls into Topor within a second or two(Time), turn the enemy into some tastey Quint/tass(Prime), rip him apart from inside(Forces), destroy his mind(Mind)/soul(Spirit)/body(Life or Matter vor Vamps), Have material grow through vital organs (Life/Matter), Dump him into a volcano or nuclear reactor(Corr) or just... use Entropy to turn him into less than dust.<br /> <br /> All of those are lvl 5 effects, Vulger with Witness most likely, so by default diff 10. 3 Quint to lower diff makes it a roll against 7. With arete 6, even a technomancer can work without his focus in his main sphere, so the mage can employ &quot;using an unneded focus&quot;, we also assume it is a personalized instrument for a sum of -2 diff, most likely it is either unique or has the appropriate Resonance to the task for another one, so the resulting roll is against 4. Then the Mage can spend a Willpower, for one free success....<br /> <br /> So the percentile chance of the mage doing something magically with the following numbers of successes and the boxes of agg damage that comes with them using the DMG table from M20 504: <div class=\"b-bbcode__table--wrapper text_table_\"><table class=\"b-bbcode__table text_table\"><tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\">0 (succ)</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\">1.28 %</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\">0</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\">1</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\">2.79</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\">2</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\">2</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\">6.60</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\">4</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\">3</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\">13.01</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\">6</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\">4</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\">19.89</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\">8</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\">5</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\">24.49</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\">10</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\">6</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\">20.17</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\">12</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\">7</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\">11.76</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\">14</td> </tr> </table></div> What a blast! Ok, That's 4.60 Successes in average.<br /> The corr is sufficiently fulfilled then (any volcano can be reached with 5 successes, with 4 you only have to have been there once), wherever you want him to be, he WILL be there next moment, and if it is only somewhere over the atlantic when you had your trip to europe but without a plane underneeth his feet - 10000 feet falling damage are NASTY.<br /> Life, Prime, Entropy and Forces (we choose to use a Fire detonation) can inflict those levels of agg damage directly and the rest... we just added 2 prime to the mix and it IS Agg damage. With 6+1 levels on the damage track, and 4+ is enough to be a potential oneshot... wait, the average damage of that attack would be 8,64 squares of agg!<br /> And then there are some spells that are just deadly without going the way of damage - seperating mind and body, extremely rapid aging of the body as it is (ca 10-25 years in a moment for 5 successes), which can be severly hampering (or for vamps send into Topor).<br /> <br /> Unless he spends another turn casting, accumulating successes (to break the treshold to age somebody living to destruction - 10-20 succ; or to affect everal targets; or to do some outlandish ammount of damage for he feels an average of 8,67 Damage is not enough), then the proposed mage can one-shot-kill most enemies, given he has better initiative.<br /> <br /> The price for this feat? 1 Paradox, no wait, let's spend 1(+) Quintessence to cancel this tiny bit of Paradox. So the Price is 3Quint/1Will/1 Paradox or 4Quint/1Will...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":9729,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9729-hira-akigi","user":"Hira Akigi","date":". 11-30-2015, 08:26 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9729-hira-akigi","name":"Hira Akigi","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"42"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-30T05:35:42-08:00","id":777100,"title":"","content":"He's working with starting characters, a min-maxed one and a sensible one, so that's right out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8760-cogliostro","name":"Cogliostro","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8760_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-30T09:20:40-08:00","id":777185,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yossarian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/769134-deadliest-supernatural-warrior-the-setup?p=777040#post777040\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Vampires can heal during combat (or other actions, as the book puts it), but they have to make a Stamina + Survival roll, difficulty 8. Page 258 of V20.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Good catch! However, I'm going to ignore that, because it seems to me that boosting abilities is almost always better that healing. +1 dex (or +1 stamina against non-aggravated) give 50% of a hit point each and every turn, and has other advantages. Also, this way I don't need to add extra choices to the already painfully slow algorithm.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4851-cheesefondue","name":"Cheesefondue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"275"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-30T09:26:00-08:00","id":777189,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">Two minor edits:<br /> <br /> EDIT: Since some character types (Vampires, Changelings, Shapeshifters) benefit from backgrounds in single combat, while others do not, no-one gets free background points (but they can purchase it with freebies).</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">EDIT: since a preliminary analysis shows that all the best strategies involve spending willpower early, I've removed the option not to do so.</span></span><br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4851-cheesefondue","name":"Cheesefondue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"275"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-30T10:20:43-08:00","id":777221,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cheesefondue</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/769134-deadliest-supernatural-warrior-the-setup?p=777185#post777185\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Good catch! However, I'm going to ignore that, because it seems to me that boosting abilities is almost always better that healing. +1 dex (or +1 stamina against non-aggravated) give 50% of a hit point each and every turn, and has other advantages. Also, this way I don't need to add extra choices to the already painfully slow algorithm.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I figured it wouldn't make too much of a difference, but the more you know!<br /> <br /> Also, this kind of number crunching in RPGs is completely anathema to me, <u><i>but I cannot get enough of this</i></u>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-30T14:10:48-08:00","id":777362,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yossarian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/769134-deadliest-supernatural-warrior-the-setup?p=777221#post777221\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, this kind of number crunching in RPGs is completely anathema to me, <u><i>but I cannot get enough of this</i></u>.</div> </div> </div> </div>I feel the same :-)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4851-cheesefondue","name":"Cheesefondue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"275"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}